The exact source-index retention proof ends at the sanitized immediate crossover boundary before its inherited canonical SMILES parse. One unselected immediate-only pool product retains all source-index atom/bond attributes there but loses the typed aromatic-core match after parsing; whole-product atomic identities and connectivity remain unchanged. The focused boundary.json records the exact identities and five passing checks. Later mutation lacks atom maps, so final core matches are explicitly structural presence and downstream absence, not provenance proof. Failed, atom-bound, duplicate and immediate identity-unchanged products are retained separately. The original first-parent source law, emitted score, parent strength, pool/feedback receipt and incumbent update are all available for the cited examples.

